<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="a11y">
  <h2 id="a11y">Accessibility and performance</h2>
  <ul class="docs-list">
    <li>Always silent (<code>muted</code>), so it can play on its own. Clips with sound belong on YouTube, not here.</li>
    <li>Plays only while at least half of it is on screen, and pauses when it scrolls away.</li>
    <li>Moving content needs a way to stop it (WCAG 2.2.2): the round button pauses and plays, and says which it will do. A visitor's pause sticks.</li>
    <li>With “reduce motion” turned on, it never starts by itself: the poster shows, with a Play button.</li>
    <li>Without JavaScript, the browser's own controls show instead.</li>
    <li><code>preload="none"</code> until it's about to play, so a page full of clips costs nothing until you scroll to them. Keep uploads under 15 MB; the build log warns above that.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
